
This is a MC simulation of a single molecule, ethanol, in the
gas phase. All internal degrees of freedom are sampled.
Equilibration = 1M; Averaging = 2M configurations.
Output is in gasout, gassum and gasplot. etoh.out is the gasout
file obtained by W. L. Jorgensen.
Time required: 
                2 minutes on a 2.4 GHz Pentium IV.
The averaging period was modified in gascmd to 4M in Sept 2011.

Execute under UNIX/Linux via:
csh -e gascmd >& log &

To run a different molecule, you can use any Z-matrices in the molecules        
directories (unchanged) or provide your own:
cp newmolecule.z gaszmat

To change the temperature, edit the gaspar file:      
 Temperature, pressure, & torsion cutoff:
   25.0000     .0000     .0000
Change the 25.0 to the desired temperature in C.

For easy execution in any directory, use the xMCGAS script:
xMCGAS molecule

dodeca10M and dodeca-flip contain results for dodecane without and with
use of the flip option for dihedral angles.
